            <ArticleTitle>Embolization of a Wiktor stent within a stent: successful nonsurgical management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of embolization of an unexpanded Wiktor stent while attempting to traverse an expanded Wiktor stent is reported. The embolized stent was subjected to longitudinal axial traction, using a balloon catheter to cause stretching and partial unraveling. This partially unraveled stent was deployed across the dissection to scaffold it. The patient had no postprocedure complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
